          "title": "You'll want to know: قانون",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قانون — qānūn — \"a law\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "يمنع القانون التدخين في المطاعم. yamnaʿu al-qānūn at-tadkhīn fī al-maṭāʿim. The law bans smoking in restaurants."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: قوانين, qawānīn."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قانون (qānūn) was borrowed from Greek kanōn, \"a measuring rod, a rule\" (EtymDB). Arabic gave it the sense of a law."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
