          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نص (naṣṣa) is built on the native Arabic root n-ṣ-ṣ, \"to raise, to set up\" (Lane). Naṣṣa is a Form I verb; from setting a thing up plainly comes stating it in writing: to stipulate."
